  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Breaking change in ISL.Providers.PDS.FakeFHIR: the public BundleMapper.FromListOfPatients method now takes a DateTimeOffset timestamp argument. FakeFHIR now gets the bundle timestamp from an internal DateTimeBroker instead of DateTimeOffset.UtcNow. The bundles the fake provider returns are otherwise unchanged.\n\t\t\tNo other public API changes since 1.0.0.9.\n\t\t\tDependency changes: in Abstractions, Hl7.Fhir.R4 6.2.0 to 6.6.0. In FHIR, Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection 10.0.8 to 10.0.13, Microsoft.IdentityModel.Tokens 8.19.1 to 8.23.0 and System.IdentityModel.Tokens.Jwt 8.18.0 to 8.23.0. In FakeFHIR, Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration, Configuration.Binder, Configuration.EnvironmentVariables, Configuration.Json and DependencyInjection 10.0.8 to 10.0.13. FHIR and FakeFHIR depend on Abstractions 1.1.0.0.",
